-- title:
--   Drinfeld formal chart at a supersingular point over general constants
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$ and a non-zero natural number $M'$ with $q \nmid M'$, and a prime $\ell$ with $\ell \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell \mid M'$.
--
--   **Level data.** $H_1$ is a subgroup of $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times$ and `hH₁` requires $H_1$ to be the intersection of [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH q M'`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelJacobian.html#L22), the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$, with the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/\ell)^\times$ (the divisibility $\ell \mid q^2M'$ coming from $\ell \mid M'$).
--
--   **The frame over general constants.** $L$ is a field of characteristic zero, $\zeta \in L$ a primitive $q$-th root of unity, $\xi \in L$ a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity with $\zeta = \xi^{\ell}$, and `hι` asserts the existence of a ring homomorphism $\iota : L \to \mathbb{C}$ with $\iota\,\xi = \exp(2\pi i/(q\ell))$. $K$ is an intermediate field of $L \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ required by `hK` to equal [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.xHFunctionField (q ^ 2 * M') H₁)`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), i.e. the $L$-subfield of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ generated by the image, under coefficientwise extension along $\mathbb{Q} \to L$, of the $q$-expansion function field of [`CohCarrier.GammaH (q ^ 2 * M') H₁`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L133). $A$ is a discrete valuation domain with $L$ as fraction field and with algebraically closed residue field, such that $q \in \mathfrak{m}_A$ and $\zeta$ lies in the image of $A$ in $L$; $A$ acts on $K$ compatibly with its action on $L$. The element $j \in K$ is required by `hj` to have Laurent series equal to the image of [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157) (the $q$-expansion $q^{-1} + 744 + \cdots$ of the modular $j$-function) under coefficientwise extension to $L$, and is non-zero. $\varpi$ generates $\mathfrak{m}_A$, and $t \in A$ satisfies $t^{q-1} = q\,w$ for some unit $w$ of $A$.
--
--   Here [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A ↥K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236) is the pushout of the two maps $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the inclusions of the chart algebras into the middle algebra, where `chartAlgFin A ↥K j` is the subalgebra of elements of $K$ integral over $A[j]$ and `chartAlgInf A ↥K j` that of elements integral over $A[j^{-1}]$, and `XFin A ↥K j` is $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the finite chart algebra. The point $z$ of this scheme is such that the germ at $z$ of the image of $\varpi$ under the structure morphism to $\operatorname{Spec} A$ — the element $\varpi z$ of the stalk pinned by `hϖz` — lies in the maximal ideal of that stalk (`hz`); $y$ is a point of `XFin A ↥K j` with `ιFin` image $z$ (`hy`).
--
--   **Supersingularity.** `hss` requires: for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi$ from the finite chart algebra to $\Omega$ with kernel $y$, the value $\varphi(j)$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), i.e. every elliptic Weierstrass curve over $\Omega$ with $j$-invariant $\varphi(j)$ has no non-zero point killed by $q$.
--
--   **The cyclotomic frame.** $L_0$ is a field of characteristic zero which is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ for $\{q\ell\}$, with $\zeta_0$ a primitive $q$-th root of unity, $\xi_0$ a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity and $\zeta_0 = \xi_0^{\ell}$; $K_0$ is [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L₀`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103) of the same function field; $A_0$ is a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L_0$ (no hypothesis on its residue field) with $q \in \mathfrak{m}_{A_0}$ and $\zeta_0$ in the image of $A_0$, acting on $K_0$ compatibly; $j_0 \in K_0$ is non-zero with Laurent series the image of [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157); $\varpi_0$ generates $\mathfrak{m}_{A_0}$; $z_0$, the stalk element $\varpi z_0$ (pinned by `hϖz₀`) lying in the maximal ideal of the stalk, and $y_0$ over $z_0$ are as before, and `hss₀` is the corresponding supersingularity requirement at $y_0$.
--
--   **Comparison data.** A ring homomorphism $i : L_0 \to L$ with $i\zeta_0 = \zeta$ and $i\xi_0 = \xi$; an $A_0$-algebra structure on $A$ whose structure map is local and injective (`hinj`) and compatible with $i$ (`hA₀A`); the relation $\mathrm{algebraMap}\,\varpi_0 = t\,w$ for some unit $w$ of $A$ (`hϖ₀t`); a ring homomorphism $c_K : K_0 \to K$ acting coefficientwise through $i$ (`hcK`) with $c_K j_0 = j$; a ring homomorphism $c$ between the finite chart algebras compatible with $c_K$ (`hc`) with $\mathrm{comap}_c\,y = y_0$ (`hcy`); and a ring isomorphism $\beta : A \otimes_{A_0} \mathrm{chartAlgFin}(A_0,K_0,j_0) \to \mathrm{chartAlgFin}(A,K,j)$ with $\beta(a \otimes b) = \mathrm{algebraMap}(a)\cdot c(b)$ (`hβ`).
--
--   **The cyclotomic witness.** $W_0$ is a discrete valuation domain, complete for the $\mathfrak{m}_{W_0}$-adic topology, $\sigma_0 : A_0 \to W_0$ a ring homomorphism with $\mathfrak{m}_{W_0} = (\sigma_0\varpi_0)$; $f_0, u_0, v_0 \in W_0[[X_0,X_1]]$ with $u_0, v_0$ units and $f_0 - (X_0X_1^{q} - X_0^{q}X_1) \in (X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$ (the Drinfeld form [`DrinfeldCurve.LocalChart.drinfeldForm q W₀`](def/DrinfeldCurve_LocalChart.html#L18)); and a ring isomorphism
--   $$e_0 : \widehat{\mathcal{O}}_{z_0} \;\xrightarrow{\ \sim\ }\; W_0[[X_0,X_1]]/\bigl(C(\sigma_0\varpi_0)\,v_0 - f_0 u_0\bigr),$$
--   where $\widehat{\mathcal{O}}_{z_0}$ is the completion of the stalk at $z_0$ for its maximal ideal.
--
--   **The riders `hriders₀`** are six clauses about this witness, stated with the abbreviations $S_0$ for the quotient power-series ring, $\mathrm{mk}S_0$ for its quotient map, $\mathrm{toC}_0$ for the map from the stalk to its completion, and $\mathrm{germ}Y_0$ for the canonical map from the finite chart algebra to the stalk at $z_0$ (through the open immersion `ιFin` and the germ map): (i) $e_0$ carries the image in the completion of the germ of $a \in A_0$ to the class of $C(\sigma_0 a)$; (ii) for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, every $L_0$-algebra automorphism $\tau$ of $K_0$ satisfying [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.IsLevelAutAt L₀ q ζ₀ q (q ^ 2 * M') H₁ γ⁻¹ K₀ τ`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelLevelAutAt.html#L29) — the condition that $\tau$ acts on quotients of integral $q$-expansions of weight-$k$ modular forms for $\mathrm{GammaH}(q^2M',H_1)$ by the slash action at the matrix `conjElemN q γ⁻¹`, read through any complex embedding sending $\zeta_0$ to $\exp(2\pi i/q)$ — preserves the finite chart algebra; (iii) if moreover $\gamma_{11} \equiv 1 \pmod{\ell}$, such a $\tau$ is the identity on the chart algebra modulo $y_0$; (iv) for such a $\gamma$ and $\tau$ preserving the chart and trivial modulo $y_0$ there are a ring automorphism $\theta$ of $S_0$, an element $c \in W_0$ and a matrix $M \in M_2(W_0)$ with: $\theta$ intertwining $e_0 \circ \mathrm{toC}_0 \circ \mathrm{germ}Y_0$ with the restriction of $\tau$; $\theta$ fixing all constants; $\theta(X_j) \equiv \sum_i M_{ij}X_i$ modulo the square of the ideal generated by the classes of $X_0, X_1$; $c^{q+1} \equiv 1$, $M_{ij} \equiv c\,\gamma_{ij}$ modulo $\mathfrak{m}_{W_0}$; $c \equiv 1$ whenever $\gamma_{11} \equiv 1 \pmod{\ell}$; and $c \not\equiv 1$ whenever $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$ and $\tau$ is not the identity; (v) for integers $a_1,b_1,a_2,b_2$ and primes $P_1,P_2$ of $S_0$, each missing one of the classes of $X_0, X_1$, each containing the class of $C(\sigma_0\varpi_0)$ and each containing an element with linear part $a_kX_0 + b_kX_1$ up to $(X_0,X_1)^2$, if $q \nmid a_1b_2 - a_2b_1$ then the contractions of $P_1$ and $P_2$ along $e_0 \circ \mathrm{toC}_0$ differ; (vi) for a prime $P$ of $S_0$ with the same non-degeneracy, containing the class of $C(\sigma_0\varpi_0)$ and an element with linear part $X_0$ up to $(X_0,X_1)^2$, an element $a$ of the finite chart algebra has $\mathrm{toC}_0(\mathrm{germ}Y_0(a))$ in the contraction of $P$ along $e_0$ if and only if every Laurent coefficient of $a$ lies in the image of $\mathfrak{m}_{A_0}$ in $L_0$.
--
--   **Conclusion.** Write $\hat A$ for the $\mathfrak{m}_A$-adic completion of $A$. There exist a ring homomorphism $\psi : W_0 \to \hat A$, power series $f, u, v \in \hat A[[X_0,X_1]]$ with $u$ and $v$ units and $f - (X_0X_1^{q} - X_0^{q}X_1) \in (X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$, and a ring isomorphism
--   $$e : \widehat{\mathcal{O}}_{z} \;\xrightarrow{\ \sim\ }\; S := \hat A[[X_0,X_1]]/\bigl(C(t)\,v - f u\bigr),$$
--   $t$ being read in $\hat A$, such that, with $\mathrm{mk}S$ the quotient map, $\mathrm{toC}$ the map from the stalk at $z$ to its completion and $\mathrm{germ}Y$ the canonical map from $\mathrm{chartAlgFin}(A,K,j)$ to that stalk, the following hold.
--
--   1. $\psi(\sigma_0 a)$ is the image of $a$ in $\hat A$ under $A_0 \to A \to \hat A$, for all $a \in A_0$.
--
--   2. $\psi(\mathfrak{m}_{W_0}) \subseteq \mathfrak{m}_{\hat A}$.
--
--   3. $f$ is the coefficientwise image of $f_0$ under $\psi$.
--
--   4. Compatibility of $e$ with $e_0$: for $x$ in the cyclotomic finite chart algebra and $s \in W_0[[X_0,X_1]]$, if $e_0$ sends the image in the completion of $\mathrm{germ}Y_0(x)$ to the class of $s$, then $e(\mathrm{toC}(\mathrm{germ}Y(c\,x))) = \mathrm{mk}S(\psi_*s)$.
--
--   5. Constants: for $a \in A$, $e$ sends the image in the completion of the germ at $z$ of $a$ (via the structure morphism to $\operatorname{Spec} A$) to the class of $C$ of the image of $a$ in $\hat A$.
--
--   6. For $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, every $L$-algebra automorphism $\tau$ of $K$ with `IsLevelAutAt L q ζ q (q ^ 2 * M') H₁ γ⁻¹ K τ` preserves $\mathrm{chartAlgFin}(A,K,j)$.
--
--   7. If in addition $\gamma_{11} \equiv 1 \pmod{\ell}$, then for such $\tau$ preserving the chart algebra, $\tau(a) - a \in y$ for every $a$ in the chart algebra.
--
--   8. For $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and such a $\tau$ preserving the chart algebra and satisfying $\tau(a) - a \in y$ for all chart elements, there exist a ring automorphism $\theta$ of $S$, an element $c \in \hat A$ and a matrix $M \in M_2(\hat A)$ such that: $\theta(e(\mathrm{toC}(\mathrm{germ}Y(a)))) = e(\mathrm{toC}(\mathrm{germ}Y(\tau a)))$ for all chart elements $a$; $\theta$ fixes $\mathrm{mk}S(C(w))$ for every $w \in \hat A$; $\theta(\mathrm{mk}S(X_j)) - \mathrm{mk}S\bigl(\sum_i C(M_{ij})X_i\bigr)$ lies in the square of the ideal generated by $\mathrm{mk}S(X_0), \mathrm{mk}S(X_1)$; $c^{q+1} - 1 \in \mathfrak{m}_{\hat A}$; $M_{ij} - c\,\gamma_{ij} \in \mathfrak{m}_{\hat A}$ for all $i,j$; if $\gamma_{11} \equiv 1 \pmod{\ell}$ then $c - 1 \in \mathfrak{m}_{\hat A}$; and if $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$ and $\tau$ is not the identity on $K$ then $c - 1 \notin \mathfrak{m}_{\hat A}$.
--
--   9. For integers $a_1,b_1,a_2,b_2$ and prime ideals $P_1, P_2$ of $S$ such that each omits $\mathrm{mk}S(X_0)$ or $\mathrm{mk}S(X_1)$, each contains $\mathrm{mk}S(C(\varpi))$ ($\varpi$ read in $\hat A$), and each contains an element of the form $a_kX_0 + b_kX_1 + h$ with $h \in (X_0,X_1)^2$, if $q \nmid a_1b_2 - a_2b_1$ then the contractions of $P_1$ and $P_2$ along $e$ followed by $\mathrm{toC}$ are distinct.
--
--   10. For a prime ideal $P$ of $S$ omitting $\mathrm{mk}S(X_0)$ or $\mathrm{mk}S(X_1)$, containing $\mathrm{mk}S(C(\varpi))$ and containing an element $X_0 + h$ with $h \in (X_0,X_1)^2$, and for $a$ in $\mathrm{chartAlgFin}(A,K,j)$: $\mathrm{toC}(\mathrm{germ}Y(a))$ lies in the contraction of $P$ along $e$ if and only if every Laurent coefficient of $a$ is the image of an element of $\mathfrak{m}_A$ in $L$.
--
--   The power series $u$ and $v$ are only constrained by being units; unlike $f$, they are not pinned to the images of $u_0$ and $v_0$. The defining element of $S$ uses the Katz–Mazur constant $t$, whereas clauses 9 and 10 use the uniformiser $\varpi$.
--
--   This is the transfer of the Drinfeld–Igusa local equation for the two-chart integral model at a supersingular point of the special fibre from the cyclotomic frame $(L_0, A_0, K_0, W_0, e_0)$, where a single witness is assumed, to an arbitrary discrete valuation ring $A$ of constants with algebraically closed residue field: the completed local ring at $z$ is a quotient $\hat A[[X_0,X_1]]/(tv - fu)$ with $f$ congruent to $X_0X_1^q - X_0^qX_1$ modulo $(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$, and the level automorphisms of $K$ coming from $\Gamma_0(M')$ act on this chart with linear part a scalar multiple of $\gamma$. It is used by the two downstream statements that extract the linear parts and the inertia behaviour of the level automorphisms at such a point, and by the statement producing the chart itself from supersingularity.
